# React Best Practices

## Component Patterns

- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement composition over inheritance
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use proper prop types with TypeScript interfaces
- Implement proper component lifecycle management

## Hooks Usage

- Follow the Rules of Hooks consistently
- Use appropriate dependency arrays in useEffect
- Implement cleanup functions when needed
- Create custom hooks for shared stateful logic
- Avoid complex nested hook dependencies

## State Management

- Use useState for simple local state
- Implement useReducer for complex state logic
- Use Context API sparingly for truly global state
- Keep state as close to usage as possible
- Avoid unnecessary state updates and re-renders

## Performance Optimization

- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement useMemo and useCallback judiciously
- Use proper key props for dynamic lists
- Implement lazy loading for code splitting
- Profile performance with React DevTools

## Component Communication

- Use props for parent-to-child communication
- Use callback props for child-to-parent communication
- Implement event bubbling patterns appropriately
- Use refs for direct DOM manipulation when needed
- Avoid prop drilling with proper architecture

## Accessibility & UX

- Use semantic HTML elements
- Implement proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Handle focus management correctly
- Provide meaningful error states and loading indicators

- Keep styles close to components
- Use proper imports/exports
- Document complex component logic
